<title>UK: German inland gas oil slips, stocks still low.</title>
<headline>German inland gas oil slips, stocks still low.</headline>
<text>
<p>(DLR/DM=1.5298)  DM/100 LTRS    DLRS/100 LTRS   LAST DM</p>
<p> HAMBURG	     40.70/41.20     26.60/26.93     41.60/42.00</p>
<p> BREMEN		40.70/41.20     26.60/26.93     41.60/42.00</p>
<p> DUISBURG	    41.40/41.80     27.06/27.32     42.50/42.80</p>
<p> FRANKFURT	   42.70/43.10     27.91/28.17     43.50/44.00</p>
<p> KARLSRUHE	   42.90/43.30     28.04/28.30     44.00/44.30</p>
<p> INGOLSTADT	  44.10/44.60     28.82/29.15     45.00/45.50</p>
<p>German inland gas oil softened on weaker London futures on Thursday. Consumer stocks inland remained below historical levels, but buyers held out for lower prices, a supplier said. The mark weakened against the dollar. -- London +44 171 542 7646</p>
</text>
